Back to Model Joints and Poses
Configure the Joints
In the next step we configure the joints of the ToolHead and of the ToolHolder. We equip the ToolHead
with a Revolute Joint and the ToolHolder with a Prismatic Joint.
• Click the ToolHead with the right mouse button and select Edit 3D Properties. Change to the Tab Joint.
We selected the Joint Settings below for the Revolute Joint.
• Click the ToolHolder with the left mouse button and press the Spacebar. Change to the tab Joint. As
the ToolHolder is to move up in the z-direction, we clicked on the button 
  next to Z. This sets the
z-direction as the Translation Direction. We then selected the Joint Settings below.
Configure the Joints
