Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Back to Model Joints and Poses
Configure the Poses
In our last step we configure the Poses of our Station.
Proceed as follows on the Tab Poses:
• Click into the background of the window of the Station with the right mouse button. Add Pose1 and
Pose2.
Configure the Poses
Plant Simulation Help 10-1115
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Click Pose1 with the left mouse button and click Edit. The dialog shows the settings which we selected
on the tab Joint.
• Click Pose2 with the left mouse button and click Edit. The dialog shows the settings we selected on the
tab Joint.
• Now that we configured joints and poses, we can program the movements in the respective controls. To
do so, we return to the simulation object and change to the tab Controls. Here we create an Entrance
Control and an Exit Control each.
Configure the Poses
10-1116 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Within the controls we define to which poses the ToolHead and the ToolHolder move.
For the Entrance Control we entered these instructions:
?._3D.Poses.moveTo("Pose2") // moves to Pose2
For the Exit Control we entered these instructions:
wait ?._3D.Poses.moveTo("Pose1") // returns to Pose1 
@.move                           // and moves the part
When you now start the simulation, you can watch how the ToolHead rotates and how the ToolHolder
moves up and then down again.
To better view the sequence, we selected the Real time factor x 3.
Configure the Poses
Plant Simulation Help 10-1117
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

You can show and hide poses with the toggle button 
 . Plant Simulation only shows a single
pose at a time. If you show a different pose, Plant Simulation first hides the pose that is already shown.
Plant Simulation moves the object to the state that corresponds to the pose. While the pose is shown and
the dialog is open, you can change the state of the pose stepwise by clicking the left or right arrow key:
Press one of the arrow keys to
• rotate the pose by 1 ° of the range from the joint settings if both limits are defined.
• move the pose by 0.1 m if at least one limit is missing when a Prismatic Joint is selected, or
• rotate the pose by 1 ° if at least one limit is missing when a Revolute Joint is selected.
The left arrow key moves the pose toward the lower limit.
The right arrow key moves the pose toward the upper limit, independent of rotation axis or translation
direction.
